c glutamate receptors and epilepsy</article-title><source>Journal of the Neurological Sciences</source><year>2006</year><volume>247</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16697014</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jns.2006.03.018</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Padayatti</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><name><surname>Pattanaik</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Ma</surname><given-names>XL</given-names></name><name><surname>van den Akker</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Structural insights into the regulation and the activation mechanism of mammalian guanylyl cyclases</article-title><source>Pharmacology &#x00026; Therapeutics</source><year>2004</year><volume>104</volume><fpage>83</fpage><lpage>99</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15518881</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.pharmthera.2004.08.003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hogg</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Novel approaches to pain relief using venom-derived peptides</article-title><source>Current Medicinal Chemistry</source><year>2006</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>3191</fpage><lpage>3201</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17168706</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Doss</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Marques</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Foister</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Chenoweth</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Dervan</surname><given-names>PB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Programmable oligomers for minor groove DNA recognition</article-title><source>Journal of the American Chemical Society</source><year>2006</year><volume>128</volume><fpage>9074</fpage><lpage>9079</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16834381</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1021/ja0621795</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vasconcelos</surname><given-names>MTSD</given-names></name><name><surname>Leal</surname><given-names>MFC</given-names></name><name><surname>van den Berg</surname><given-names>CMG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Influence of the nature of the exudates released by different marine algae on the growth, trace metal uptake and exudation of Emiliania huxleyi in natural seawater</article-title><source>Marine Chemistry</source><year>2002</year><volume>77</volume><fpage>187</fpage><lpage>210</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0304-4203(01)00087-1</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>